# Read by `op run --env-file` (see bin/release and Hecks::Release::Runner).
# This holds an op:// REFERENCE, not a secret — safe to commit. `op run` resolves
# it at run time (unlocked by Touch ID) and injects it into `npm publish`'s one
# subprocess only. npm expands ${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN} in a throwaway user config, so
# the token is never written to disk.
#
# The token is the concealed field "publish token" on the "npmjs.com" item in
# the Hecks vault. Edit the vault, item or field here if yours differ.
#
# It must be a granular token with "Bypass two-factor authentication" enabled,
# scoped Read and write to the @hecks scope: the account's second factor is a
# passkey, so a token that requires a one-time code cannot publish (npm answers
# EOTP). The publish also passes --auth-type=web, so if npm does ask for a
# passkey approval it prints a link and waits; that is the interactive fallback.
NODE_AUTH_TOKEN="op://Hecks/npmjs.com/publish token"
